---
#1650: `String.replace` inserts its replacement literally. JS expands `$&`, `$1`,
`` $` ``, `$'` and `$$` in a string replacement; the emitted function replacer
means none of them is special.
---
commons demo.text

fn rep(s: String, target: String, with: String) -> String {
  s.replace(target, with)
}
